WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.560
Two common TFSA habits that work while saving could backfire in retirement, according to Motley Fool Canada. This is Modern Investing Techniques, episode 187. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:44.440
The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,652, down 0.3%. The TSX composite ended at 35,236, down 0.6%.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:50.140
Canadian dollar weakness is expected in the near term before a potential rebound in 2027,

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.720
as Bank of Canada rate hikes narrowed the gap with the Fed.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:01:04.560
About 16 days ago we picked LMT on a government contract award providing near-term revenue visibility and it closed up 0.61%.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:11.080
That move showed how contract visibility can buffer single-name positions even when broader rotation is active.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:17.880
The S&amp;P 500 now shows only 32.5% of its constituents beating the index.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:24.260
Energy names on the TSX have shown relative resilience in recent sessions, even as miners

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:29.940
weighed on the broader index. Support and resistance levels drawn from horizontal price history

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.260
provide a more objective framework than trend lines. They rely on repeated tests at the

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:43.540
same price rather than subjective slope. Today's market shows the S&amp;P 500 with only 32.5% of stocks

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:49.720
beating the index. Clear horizontal levels help separate noise from genuine rotation signals in

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:55.320
that environment. Investors can implement this by pulling a two-year daily chart in a platform

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:01.680
like TradingView, or the Free Options Play Charting tool. Mark every prior high and low that saw

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:07.960
at least two touches. Then wait for a close beyond the level on volume above the 20-day average before

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:14.540
acting. This approach worked well during the 2022 bear market when many growth names respected the

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:20.680
same horizontal ceilings on multiple retests before breaking lower. The risk is that low volume

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:27.760
brakes can produce false signals. Pairing the level with a volume filter reduces whip saws. Horizontal

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:33.840
lines also allow clearer invalidation points because a brake is defined by a specific price rather

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.680
than a shifting slope. Canadian investors can apply the same method to T.S.X. names in

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:46.740
their T.F.S.A. by using the same two-year look-back window. Require the volume confirmation before entry.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:52.780
The method aligns with active rules that require volume above the 20-day average before committing

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:59.820
capital to names already in sector rotation. Imagine you have been maxing your T.F.S.A. every year

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.020
by treating it as a pure growth vehicle.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.480
You never withdraw even small amounts to rebalance.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.300
The mechanism that changes that retirement

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.180
is the contribution room itself.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.020
Once you stop earning eligible income,

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.980
the annual room stops growing.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.880
Yet many investors continue aggressive equity allocations

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.700
that were optimal during accumulation.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.380
The pro tip is to run a simple five minute projection

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.660
in your brokerage's retirement calculator.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:33.540
later. Use your current TFS-A balance, expected withdrawal rate, and a conservative 7% equity

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:39.100
return assumption. See whether the same allocation still fits a decumulation glide path.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:44.760
The misconception to avoid is assuming the habits that maximized room during working years

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.540
will automatically serve you once the contribution tap turns off.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:54.480
Withdrawal sequencing also matters because early retirement years often coincide with higher

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:00.500
spending needs before government benefits begin. Rebalancing within the TFSA can preserve

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:05.920
room for future contributions if small withdrawals are made strategically before age 71.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:13.080
The shift from accumulation to decumulation changes the optimal risk level. Sequence of returns risk

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:19.120
becomes the dominant concern rather than long-term compounding alone. This week's practice investment

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:25.300
applies a valuation screen first, then adds a same-day volume check as required by active rules.

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:34.380
The pick is BTE.TO, Batex Energy. It is a TSX-listed energy name showing resilient cash flow

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:41.680
amid commodity volatility. The strategy family is valuation. The hold period is five sessions from entry.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.820
Invalidation comes if the stock closes the week below its 50-day moving average.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:52.480
average. That breach would invalidate the valuation support thesis. The catalyst is the

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:58.240
Canadian dollar outlook and energy sector resilience noted in the BNN Bloomberg market outlook.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:03.780
Technical setup shows price action holding above the 50-day moving average on the daily

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:10.020
chart with volume near the 20-day average. Risk assessment sets a maximum acceptable loss

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:14.360
plus of 8% if the 50-day moving average is breached intraday.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.500
The target is plus 3% to plus 7% over the 5-session window.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:25.520
Confidence is medium because the valuation buffer is present and the macro backdrop for

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:29.740
energy is constructive, yet volume confirmation is only average.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:35.260
This pick applies the valuation screen first, then adds a same-day volume check.

